{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tracker drift tracker drift","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md","fileName":"Tracker Drift.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tracker Drift","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Tracking and Registration]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Tracking and Registration","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tracker drift tracker drift","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md","fileName":"Tracker Drift.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tracker Drift","heading":"Tracker Drift","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Tracker drift is accumulated pose error that grows as relative measurements are integrated over time. Gyroscopes, accelerometers, odometers, and incremental visual trackers can follow short-term change well while their estimate gradually departs from the physical reference.\n\nAn absolute measurement or recognized location can correct the accumulated error. Sensor fusion and visual loop closure use such evidence to retain responsive local tracking without allowing the reference frame to wander indefinitely.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Tracking and Registration","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tracker drift tracker drift","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tracker Drift.md","fileName":"Tracker Drift.md","f